# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository and in the working copy,
# independent of each developer's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# The generated data files are written by the database builder with LF
# line breaks plus a trailing PHP_EOL (CRLF on Windows), which makes them
# mixed-ending files. The explicit `text` attribute makes git normalize
# them reliably, where `text=auto` would skip files with mixed endings.
* text=auto eol=lf
data/*.json text eol=lf
*.php text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
